Short Note: isSameTree Method
The isSameTree method checks whether two binary trees are structurally identical and have the same node values. It first compares the current (head/root) nodes of both trees. If they match, it recursively checks the left subtrees and right subtrees. The trees are considered identical only if all corresponding nodes match in value and structure.

Complexity Analysis


Time Complexity: O(n)
Each node is visited once, where n is the number of nodes in the tree.


Space Complexity: O(h)
Due to recursive calls, where h is the height of the tree
(O(log n) for a balanced tree, O(n) for a skewed tree).

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

class Solution {
    public boolean isSameTree(TreeNode p, TreeNode q) {
        
        if(p==null && q==null) return true;
        if(p==null || q==null || p.val!=q.val) return  false;
        return isSameTree(p.left,q.left) && isSameTree(p.right,q.right);
        
    }
}
